{"agent_id":"pp3g-OgQA-continuation-of-the-464-interop-probe-prior-run-pp3g","agent_seq":7,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T03:15:10.864412712Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4f1f452c-4304-4e51-9e8f-e78f9d441b03","comment_uuid":"93074298-38df-40f1-9f54-93d51b8b0a7f","author":"pp3g-OgQA-continuation-of-the-464-interop-probe-prior-run-pp3g","content":"[PROGRESS] state=working completed=T5b DONE: v2 permission model = Ruleset[{action,resource,effect allow|deny|ask}] (openapi Permission.Rule schema); in practice: deny=>tool hidden from toolset entirely (model reports 'no shell tool'); ask=>also hidden statically BUT runtime asks still fire - headless w/o --auto AUTO-REJECTS fail-closed, stderr 'permission requested: external_directory (/etc/*); auto-rejecting', exit!=0, NEVER hangs; --auto approves non-denied asks (shell+/etc read OK exit0); default no-rules=allow; native fs tools path-scoped to project (external_directory action) vs shell separate action surface next=T5c live API drive loop blocker=none","created_at":"2026-08-25T03:15:10.853156464Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:Ky5Z4VB8wELdMm04hGcbJKD3vSZrafxZ5qj3Y0L6OY4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg5pI05tQ2laOzeu3+4/1o7znykAauZGV+shMNBQFxANAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA9EwqiM5f6GJ2VoFhJntxbZAFQfBWupSDuMmx5Yoo2Aufrx/3FwqRnMoUaCjKVNqtCkgH5AtRXODdXr6x7PGLBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:Ky5Z4VB8wELdMm04hGcbJKD3vSZrafxZ5qj3Y0L6OY4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg5pI05tQ2laOzeu3+4/1o7znykAauZGV+shMNBQFxANAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQInIDLo+kqNrse0WlreV/+RS6SvtQIa8lWhBfEFd0NROkfHdI9AN7JWtziC9FNqnmA3bNNMe3v4Thfub0KDFmAs="}
{"agent_id":"pp3g-OgQA-continuation-of-the-464-interop-probe-prior-run-pp3g","agent_seq":8,"timestamp":"2026-08-25T03:22:07.548094456Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4f1f452c-4304-4e51-9e8f-e78f9d441b03","comment_uuid":"b9abb993-2af1-4d2c-acf6-08843385b432","author":"pp3g-OgQA-continuation-of-the-464-interop-probe-prior-run-pp3g","content":"RESULT — VERDICT BLOCK (crosslink-drives-v2-headless, opencode2 v0.0.0-beta-17963; runs pp3g-KXdh T1-T4 + pp3g-OgQA T5a-T5d; raw evidence + reconstruction recipe committed at docs/research/registry/Interop-Probe-Evidence-Pack-464.md, commit 7e938063)\n\nVERDICT: WORKS-WITH-CAVEATS\n\nCoordination layer CAN drive v2 headlessly end-to-end today — both CLI (opencode2 run --format json --model <id>) and HTTP API (session→prompt→wait→message loop proven live) — but five caveats gate a naive fleet migration.\n\nWHY: every claim below was executed against the live beta binary in this environment, with discriminating tests where global-vs-project behavior could be confounded.\nWHAT: command outputs + openapi schema captures under /tmp/opencode/probe-v2/, mirrored to the committed evidence pack.\nHOW CERTAIN: evidence-based (all reproduced at least once; core loop twice). Not proven: behavior under service restarts/fleet-scale concurrency.\n\nMIGRATION NOTES (each with evidence):\n1. WRAPPER CHANGES — kickoff wrapper must move from fork CLI to: opencode2 run [--standalone] --model opencode-go/<id> --format json [--auto]. JSON stream carries sessionID per event (T3). No prompt_async endpoint exists (0 matches in 100-route openapi) — programmatic drivers use POST /api/session/{id}/prompt (async submit, delivery:steer) + POST /api/session/{id}/wait (204 on idle) + GET /api/session/{id}/message; push consumers use GET /api/event (SSE + heartbeats). Live loop returned exact prompted string PROBE-T5C-DRIVE-OK.\n2. STORE COEXISTENCE — clean. v2 writes ~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.db table session_v2 (my API-driven session id verified present there by direct sqlite read); v1-fork keeps its own opencode-fork-pp3g.db (627 sessions, untouched). Both fleets can run side-by-side during migration.\n3. PLUGIN GAP (highest risk) — v2 does NOT execute global plugins: (a) no dir fallback — temp canary in ~/.config/opencode/plugins/ stayed silent while project canary fired in same run; (b) config plugin[] is parsed (visible in GET /api/config source stack) but not executed — grok + cloudflare-ai-gateway/deepseek/openai models are VISIBLE in v2 catalog but filtered in v1 fork where plugin.ts runs its FORBIDDEN-model blacklist (#347). Any global-plugin guarantee (provider bans, model blacklists, provider suppression) silently vanishes on v2. Project-level .opencode/plugins/ DO auto-load (canary factory-invoked marker).\n4. PERMISSION SHAPE — v2 uses permissions:[{action,resource,effect allow|deny|ask}] rulesets (openapi Permission.Rule; attaches to Config + per-Agent), NOT the fork permission object-map. Practice: deny ⇒ tool removed from toolset entirely; ask ⇒ hidden statically AND runtime asks (action external_directory for fs paths outside project root) auto-REJECT in headless without --auto (stderr: 'permission requested: external_directory (/etc/*); auto-rejecting'; fail-closed, never hangs — safe for unattended fleets); --auto approves non-denied asks; no rules = default allow. Wrapper must either pass --auto or ship project permission configs; silent-tool-removal under deny/ask can make agents flail (observed 'Unknown tool search' pivots).\n5. SERVICE LIFETIME — default CLI connects to a long-lived background service (serve --service); plugins/config load ONCE per service lifetime (project canary fired on first run only), and plugin code executes with the SERVICE cwd (/home/claude-code), not the session directory. Config changes require service restart to take effect; use --standalone for hermetic per-run isolation if freshness matters.\n\nWHAT-NOT-TESTED: agent/subagent dispatch via POST /api/session/{id}/agent and inbox queue/steer semantics beyond single steer; programmatic permission reply flow (once/always/reject); whether --auto overrides explicit deny rules (help text implies no; unverified); MCP server functionality under v2 beyond spawn logs; worktree endpoints; multi-session concurrency limits of one background service; service-restart plugin reload.","created_at":"2026-08-25T03:22:07.538434336Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:Ky5Z4VB8wELdMm04hGcbJKD3vSZrafxZ5qj3Y0L6OY4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg5pI05tQ2laOzeu3+4/1o7znykAauZGV+shMNBQFxANAAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAnwYvey/2/x0RtMy9yiqRZxiU4FHxJ+7+gMATbV+niBVA5K7MsPiixgv2TxjIpi6MVtpvXAgD7GX49QRW92J0AQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:Ky5Z4VB8wELdMm04hGcbJKD3vSZrafxZ5qj3Y0L6OY4","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAg5pI05tQ2laOzeu3+4/1o7znykAauZGV+shMNBQFxANAAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKNvyOAcXdS7UCxRWGiny0QdPApVd2BPeeOSVwk+jK6amJFpmzetEosvW1mzfNugK2OIK5M6PgB1nCvFWxHrQgQ="}
